\section{Doing it a step at a time}{


Every stage is its own function, so a run can be inspected, altered or
repeated at any point:

\describe{
\item{\code{\link[=read_analysis_dataset]{read_analysis_dataset()}}}{read and profile a \code{.csv} / \code{.xlsx}
dataset.}
\item{\code{\link[=read_loa_workbook]{read_loa_workbook()}}}{read every recognised sheet of the LoA
workbook, interpreting nothing.}
\item{\code{\link[=check_analysis_inputs]{check_analysis_inputs()}}}{validate the workbook against the
dataset. Reports errors, warnings and variable coverage, and never
stops.}
\item{\code{\link[=build_analysis_spec]{build_analysis_spec()}}}{turn the workbook into the single internal
description of a run.}
\item{\code{\link[=run_analysis_spec]{run_analysis_spec()}}}{run a specification.}
\item{\code{\link[=run_group_analysis_pipeline]{run_group_analysis_pipeline()}}}{the analysis engine itself, callable
directly with plain R arguments and no workbook at all.}
\item{\code{\link[=ak_export_results]{ak_export_results()}}}{write a completed run to a folder.}
}
}

